    <p>
      <b>Description</b>
    </p>
    <p>Applies the square-root variant selected by the <code>Function</code> parameter, element-wise, with scalar expansion for vector signals.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Function</b>
    </p>
    <p><code>sqrt</code>: square root <code>sqrt(u)</code> (a negative input yields NaN on the real path).</p>
    <p><code>signedSqrt</code>: signed square root <code>sign(u)*sqrt(|u|)</code> (always real).</p>
    <p><code>rSqrt</code>: reciprocal square root <code>1/sqrt(u)</code>.</p>
    <p>This page describes the native runtime behavior observed in the module C++ sources. Declared phases indicate when the simulation engine calls the block.</p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
